    "body": "fix on issue/1174-chuck-limit-work-spindle-only · PR #1191 · pinned by lathe_workholding_live (a_10000_rpm_cross_drill_is_not_judged_by_a_100_rpm_chuck, a_c_section_is_judged_by_its_c_rate_never_by_the_live_tools_rpm, a_c_section_on_an_unrated_c_is_refused_only_under_a_stated_limit), lathe_workholding_rpm::a_3000_rpm_g97_turning_op_under_a_2000_rpm_chuck_is_still_refused_by_name · merges when reviewed. Kind split read from fanuc-lathe.cps: turning + lathe axial drill drive the work spindle (G97/G96 M03); a C section (LiveTool) gives S to the live spindle and is judged by the machine's C rate (unrated C refused while a limit is stated); a cross drill is a driven radial tool with the work held - not judged. Follow-up found: #1190 (mill op on a mill-turn without C opens with G97 S M03).",
