    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T12:06:13Z",
    "body": "Re-rated `P0` after the high-tier review of PR #1191 (review comment on that PR, head 81e4cb01): the limit also FAILS OPEN. Reproduced: a Drill with one axial hole at XY 0,0 at 8000 rpm, setup with a 2000 rpm chuck limit, mill-turn machine - the gate finds nothing and the program posts `G97 S8000 M03` / `G83 Z6`: the chuck is spun at four times its stated limit. On a pure lathe the same setup is refused by name. Cause: `work_speed` (`crates/app/src/setup_workholding.rs`) falls back to `spindle_law::turns`, which counts an axial Drill only on a pure lathe. It is older than PR #1191 (main has the gap since #1058), but it is the dangerous direction of the same rule, so it is fixed in the same PR: the fix round is with the original worker. Bore, mill Thread and Probe on centre and other paths that stay on the meridian are expected to hit the same gap.",
