    "body": "second review fix on issue/1174-chuck-limit-work-spindle-only · PR #1191 head c08685ea (stacked on #1202) · the limit is judged for the post that runs (post::dialect::work_voice + lathe_voice::voice_of), whatever machine is mounted · pinned by lathe_workholding_kinds (a_lathe_post_is_held_to_the_chuck_whatever_machine_is_mounted, a_mill_post_drives_the_tool_spindle_so_the_chuck_limit_does_not_judge_it, an_undeclared_script_takes_the_stricter_reading, a_milling_script_on_a_plain_lathe_still_turns_the_work, a_speed_a_hair_over_the_chuck_prints_a_decimal) · merges when reviewed. No P7 follow-up filed for 'a mill-turn through a mill post is refused too widely': with this rule a milling post on a mill-turn is no longer judged, so that over-reach is gone.",
